  "sources": [
    "https://support.apple.com/en-us/102650",
    "https://support.apple.com/en-us/102646"
  ],
  "note": "Apple writes Command as Cmd, Option as Alt and Control as Ctrl here. The Mac Delete key (backwards delete) is written Backspace, which is the key the chord grammar names. Finder-window shortcuts live in catalog/finder.json. Left out because the chord grammar cannot express them: every Fn shortcut (Fn-A, Fn-C, Fn-D, Fn-E, Fn-H, Fn-N, Fn-Q, Fn-Fn, Fn-Shift-A, Fn-F11, Fn-Delete, Fn with the arrow keys), every Power button and Touch ID combination, the hardware-key combinations (Brightness, Volume, Keyboard Brightness, Mission Control), Command+Command (press twice), Control-Shift held for Dock magnification (modifier-only), the open-ended \"Arrow keys\" and \"Control-Arrow keys\" rows, and every click/double-click/drag shortcut.",
